# cm-benchmark — core rules

Spatial-cognition QA benchmark for VLMs. Items = frames from SPOC/AI2-THOR
exports + question. 8 constructs, 4 classes (configs/taxonomy.yaml).

## Sources of truth (read only when the task needs them)
- Construct definitions: configs/taxonomy.yaml
- Every quality-affecting value: configs/generation.yaml (never hardcode)
- Pipeline and modules: docs/architecture.md
- Parameter justifications: docs/parameters_report.md

## Invariants (never break)
1. Answers come only from exported metadata; every item has answer_source.
2. Generation, validation and scoring are deterministic code; no LLM judges answers.
3. FREEZE is one-way: evaluation never edits or regenerates items.
4. Questions never state the answer, a direction or a move.
5. Confusable objects (obj-synset rule) are disambiguated by proximity or mark;
   never by a direction.

## How to work
- Make the smallest change that does the task. Do not refactor unrelated code.
- Read only the files the task touches. Don't explore the repo unless asked.
- Run only the relevant tests; rerun pilots only when the prompt asks.
- Keep reports short: a table or a few lines, no restating the prompt.
- If a request conflicts with these rules or the docs, ask before acting.